A||||5||Groot||Opening front-hood||||8
Z||000000||Groot||10-18-1999||03:15 PM||||Hi,<P>Just bought a 84-2M4 .... there is no<BR>way i can open the front-hood.<BR>Applying a lot of force to the cable<BR>( or spare cable ) does not work.<P>I can hear the lock moving a little, but<BR>not far enought to open it.<P>Every suggestion is welcome<P>Egbert||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||10-18-1999||06:17 PM||||try pushing down over the latch while pulling the release.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||10-18-1999||06:33 PM||||Ogre, you beat me to it.  I was going to suggest if pushing down doesn't help, have someone sit over the latch.  If the paint is good, then be careful you don't scratch it all up.||||reg||14
Z||000004||theogre||10-18-1999||10:36 PM||||If that does work spray the hell out of it with some kind of oil.<P>Some times the type of latch used in the hood, and trunk, need a good jolt to jar loose. If pushing/sitting on it doesn't free it, try placing a folded towel under a peice of 2X6x12 or large wood stock over the latch. then wack the wood block a few times LIGHTLY with a heavy object. That will rattle the latch guts. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||10-19-1999||12:07 PM||||Ok perhaps this will work (I haven't tried it myself so no guarantees here). The latch that holds the hood down is exactly in the middle about 5" from the back end of the hood (the end nearest the front window). If you look under the hood (between the windshield wipers) you are not able to see the latch because it's obstructed by the tube for the washer fluid. But you should be able to get a screwdriver in the latch and open it. Just get a long screwdriver, and gently stick it under the hood exactly in the middle (be careful not to damage the washer fluid tube!). You should feel the latch. Move the screwdriver sideways a bit until you can stick it in even further. Then move the screwdriver to the left and with a little luck that will open up the front hood.<P>Like I said, I haven't tried this so I might have overlooked an obstacle which makes this whole procedure impossible... But you could at least give it a try.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Groot||10-20-1999||04:06 AM||||Hi,<P>Ok, i think that the method with the<BR>screw-driver is most likely to work<BR>as pulling and pushing the hood itself<BR>combined with cable-force did not<BR>work out.<P>I will try it in the next weekend !<BR>Now i will spray WD40 in it to<BR>make the rust weak.<P>Thanks for now .. i come back with<BR>good news i hope !<P>Egbert<P>||||reg||7
